<title>USA: Ted Turner says News Corp lawsuit is frivolous.</title>
<headline>Ted Turner says News Corp lawsuit is frivolous.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ted Turner, soon to be vice chairman of Time Warner Inc, dismissed as frivolous on Thursday a News Corp Ltd anti-trust lawsuit against himself and Time Warner.</p>
<p>&quot;That frivolous piece of junk,&quot; Turner told reporters when asked about the lawsuit after Time Warner shareholders approved a $6.7 billion merger with his company, Turner Broadcasting System Inc.</p>
<p>News Corp on Wednesday filed a lawsuit charging Time Warner with violations of U.S. anti-trust law for refusing to carry its freshly launced Fox News Channel on its New York City cable systems reaching 1.2 million homes.</p>
<p>The systems already carry all-news rivals of Fox News, including Cable News Network being acquired by Time Warner.</p>
<p>-- Michael Connor 212-859-1713</p>
